<title>NETHERLANDS: SOCCER-DUTCHMAN ISRAEL TO COACH GHANA.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-DUTCHMAN ISRAEL TO COACH GHANA.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutchman Rinus Israel has signed a contract to coach the Ghanean national team until the 1998 Word Cup, Dutch ANP news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>Israel, who won 47 caps for the Netherlands and was in Feyenoord's 1970 European Cup-winning side, has more recently been coach of the Dutch under-21 squad.</p>
<p>Israel replaces Sam Arday.</p>
